## SMR and MR analysis of UC with PSC
IVW-MR analysis also found evidence for the casual association between OPRL1, BTRC, FBXL17, SIRT1, and PML with UC along with PSC (OR 0.523, $95\%C\mathrm{I}$ 0.437–0.624; OR 0.469, $95\%C\mathrm{I}$ 0.245–0.896; OR 2.480, $95\%C\mathrm{I}$ 1.748–3.517; OR 1.277, $95\%C\mathrm{I}$ 1.169–1.395; OR 2.665, $95\%C\mathrm{I}$ 1.232–5.765, respectively) (Fig.  3, Supple­ mentary Table 3). IVW-MR analysis provides additional support for a potential protective effect of OPRL1 and BTRC against the development of UC with PSC, while also suggesting FBXL17, SIRT1, and PML as potential risk factors. In IVW-MR analysis, horizontal pleiotropy was observed in FBXL17 and BTRC $_{\it P=0.011}$ ; $\scriptstyle P=0.013$ ).
